# Disposition (DESIGN.md §8): how an observer, a faction or a character, regards a character.
# Five components, each within -100..100, are weighted and added up: affinity (how close the
# alignments are), standing, kinship, faction opinion and modifiers.
load content/sample
disposition city_watch player --explain
# The Temple loves its own priestess: affinity 45.34, standing 40, kinship 50 × 0.5, clamped.
assert disposition temple sister_mira == 100.00 (friendly)
# Ash belongs to the Temple's enemy: affinity -32.15, kinship -90 × 0.5.
assert disposition temple brother_ash == -77.15 (unfriendly)
disposition city_watch vex --explain
# Hale's Watch is allied with the Temple: affinity 14.75, kinship 60 × 0.5.
assert disposition captain_hale sister_mira == 44.75 (friendly)
# A character judges by their own lights: Vex sees the neutral player as barely neutral.
assert disposition vex player == 1.23 (neutral)
# The worked example (DESIGN.md §8.2): two thefts from a merchant, then a fine.
act player steal --target merchant_ava
act player steal --target merchant_ava
outcome fined_by_watch player
disposition captain_hale player --explain
assert disposition player temple == error: a disposition's subject must be a character

# Bands are content: this world adds hostile below unfriendly.
load crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/hostile
disposition temple brother_ash --explain
